- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/fractalsample.html
- Summary (EN): Fractal Sample builds a fractal from a source layer by sampling that input at rising frequencies and blending the results into a continuous pattern of shrinking copies. Its randomization options add organic or inorganic variation, suiting effects such as algae, frost, or kaleidoscopic patterns.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Fractal Sample construit une fractale à partir d'une couche source, en superposant des copies de plus en plus petites de celle-ci.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: sets the output size and controls metadata", "source: original layer to which the fractal effect is applied", "octaves (optional): multiplies Max Octaves", "lacunarity (optional): multiplies Lacunarity", "roughness (optional): multiplies Roughness"]

- Key parameters: ["Max Octaves: number of octaves combined", "Lacunarity: scale factor applied to each octave", "Roughness: amplitude scale applied to each successive octave", "Blend Mode: Add, Subtract, Maximum or Over", "Maintain Tileable: clamps or rounds certain values (for example Lacunarity to integers) to help preserve tiling", "Seed: random values for Jitter, Angle and Flip", "Jitter: random position offset applied to each octave", "Angle: rotation per octave, applied incrementally (Per Octave) or randomly within a range (Random)", "Random Flip X and Random Flip Y: randomly flip each octave on an axis", "Post-processing (Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum): adjusts output values, run in the order listed"]

- Caveats: ["Maintain Tileable does not create tileability; it only preserves tiling if the source input already tiles", "The Over blend mode is valid only when the input is RGBA", "Complement assumes values in the 0 to 1 range, so other ranges can produce negative or out-of-range values", "Fold has no effect when all values are positive"]

